BABIV
PENCEGAHAN
Bagian Kesatu
Pemerintah Kabupaten Pasal13 (1) Upaya yang dilakukan Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam rangka mencegah teIjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak Perempuan meliputi:
a. penyelenggaraan sosialisasi mengenai pencegahan kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. penyediaan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan;
c. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam pemulihan dan reintegrasi; d. pengembangan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan;
e. pengembangan program pemberdayaan keluarga;
f. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak di bidang pemberdayaan Perempuan; dan
g. penyediaan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk Perempuan.
(2) Upaya yang dilakukan Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam rangka mencegah teIjadinya pelanggaran hak Anak meliputi:
a. pencegahan tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan; b. pengembangan sekolah ramah Anak;
c. mendorong peningkatan partisipasi anak melalui pembentukan Forum Anak;
d. penyediaan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak;
e. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam layanan pemulihan dan reintegrasi Anak korban kekerasan;
f. pengembangan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak;
g. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak di bidang perlindungan Anak; dan
h. mendorong pembentukan Kabupaten Layak Anak.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV
PREVENTION
Part One
Regency Government
Article 13
(1) Efforts undertaken by the Regency Government in order to prevent violations of Women's rights include:
  a. conducting socialization regarding prevention of violence against Women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
  b. provision of guidelines on handling acts of violence against Women;
  c. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration;
  d. development of an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against Women;
  e. development of family empowerment programs;
  f. strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in Women's empowerment; and
  g. provision of public facilities that are comfortable and safe for Women.
(2) Efforts undertaken by the Regency Government in order to prevent violations of Children's rights include:
  a. prevention of acts of violence against Children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
  b. development of child-friendly schools;
  c. encouraging increased participation of children through the establishment of Children's Forums;
  d. provision of guidelines on handling acts of violence against Children;
  e. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration services for child victims of violence;
  f. development of an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against Children;
  g. strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in Child protection; and
  h. encouraging the establishment of a Child-Friendly Regency.

