BABVI
PENANGANAN
Bagian Kesatu
Penanganan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan Pasal40 Pelaksanaan penanganan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan meliputi: a. penanganan pengaduan korban kekerasan;
b. pelayanan kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dan
e. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
Pasal41 (1) Pelaksanaan penanganan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 40 dilaksanakan melalui pelayanan terpadu.
(2) Pelayanan terpadu bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)menggunakan prinsip:
a. responsif gender;
b. non diskriminasi;
c. hubungan setara dan menghormati;
d. menjaga kerahasiaan;
e. memberi rasa aman dan nyaman;
f. menghargai perbedaan individu;
g. tidak menghakimi;
h. menghormati pilihan dan keputusan korban;
i. peka terhadap latar belakang dan kondisi korban dan pemakaian bahasa yang sesuai dan dimengerti oleh korban;
j. cepat dan sederhana;
k. empati;
I. pemenuhan hak Perempuan dan Anak; dan
m. tidak dipungut biaya.
Pasal42 Pelayanan penanganan pengaduan korban kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak dilaksanakan oleh:
a. rumah sakit;
b. puskesmas;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Unit Pelayanan Perempuan dan Anak (UPPA);
e. Rumah Perlindungan Trauma Center (RPTC);
f. Rumah Perlindungan Sosial Anak (RPSA);
g. Women Crisis Centre (WCC)
h. Badan Penasehat Pembinaan dan Pelestarian Perkawinan (BP4); i. Kepolisian;
j. Kejaksaan;
k. Pengadilan;
I. Lembaga Bantuan Hukum (LBH);dan
m.Lembaga Perlindungan Anak (LPA).
Pasal43 (1) Pengaduan tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 42 dapat dilakukan oleh pelapor yang terdiri atas:
a.Korban;
b.Keluarga;
c. Masyarakat; dan Iatau
d.organisasi kemasyarakatan di bidang perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak.
(2) Pelapor sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat melakukan pengaduan: a. secara langsung;
b. melalui telepon; dan
c. melalui surat.
(3) Seiain penanganan pengaduan yang disampaikan oieh pelapor, petugas pada lembaga pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 42 berwenang melakukan penanganan korban kekerasan Perempuan dan Anak yang diperoleh melalui informasi lainnya.
(4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai tata cara pelayanan penanganan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)dan ayat (2)diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati

translated_text:
CHAPTER VI
HANDLING
Part One
Handling of Women and Children Victims of Violence Article 40 The implementation of handling of Women and Children victims of violence includes: a. handling of complaints from victims of violence;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. law enforcement and legal assistance; and
e. repatriation and social reintegration.
Article 41 (1) The implementation of handling of Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in Article 40 is carried out through integrated services.
(2) Integrated services for Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) use the principles of:
a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relations;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitive to the background and conditions of victims and the use of appropriate language understood by victims;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy;
l. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children; and
m. free of charge.
Article 42 Complaint handling services for victims of violence against Women and Children are carried out by:
a. hospitals;
b. community health centers;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Women and Children Service Units (UPPA);
e. Trauma Center Shelter Houses (RPTC);
f. Children's Social Shelter Houses (RPSA);
g. Women Crisis Centre (WCC)
h. Advisory Board for Marriage Guidance and Preservation (BP4);
i. Police;
j. Prosecutor's Office;
k. Courts;
l. Legal Aid Institutions (LBH); and
m. Child Protection Institutions (LPA).
Article 43 (1) Complaints of acts of violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 42 may be made by reporters consisting of:
a. Victims;
b. Family;
c. Community; and/or
d. community organizations in the field of protection of Women and Children.
(2) Reporters as referred to in paragraph (1) may file complaints: a. directly;
b. by telephone; and
c. by letter.
(3) In addition to handling complaints submitted by reporters, officers at service institutions as referred to in Article 42 are authorized to handle Women and Children victims of violence obtained through other information.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for complaint handling services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are regulated by Regent Regulation

